+---
+description: "See the current task's steps mapped to Daniel's business modules, and which of the nine modules the task has used, in a read-only rail collapsed to a 48px strip."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-capability-map
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+Watch the current task without leaving the conversation. The rail stays collapsed to a 48px strip until opened; the 320px panel then shows two blocks only: the task's step path (each step is a business action on a Daniel module) and a panorama of the nine modules with a call count and one of three states — 未用 / 使用中 / 已用. It deliberately does not list every capability: that reference belongs in a separate guide, not in the live rail. The rail is read-only, follows one task at a time, and resets when the user starts a new task.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)
+- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+The Web application bundle mounts this Client plugin as the `ui-capability-map` roster row; it injects `slots`, `locale`, and `sessions` and occupies the frame's `shell.rail` column. The frame sizes that track (48px strip or 320px panel), owns the open request, and passes `{ open, onToggle }` to the occupant. A composition that wants the rail only needs that roster row; no config field exists.
+
+### Regenerate the module map
+
+The shipped data is generated from the Daniel workflow map and checked in, so the browser never reads a workspace file:
+
+```bash
+node packages/client/ui-capability-map/scripts/build-module-map.mjs \
+  --from "/path/to/daniel-bot/app/workflow-map.json"
+```
+
+The script keeps exactly nine business modules, maps every published command to one authored business action, folds `检索词清单` into 红人检索, renames each module to Daniel's own wording with an English name beside it (`账号与盘点 / Account`, `品牌档案 / Brand Profile`, …), drops the operations modules, and writes `src/client/module-map.generated.ts`. It fails instead of writing a table that misses a module, leaks an operations command, ships a module without both names, or ships a display string with a command name, path, underscore, or ASCII letters (the fallback sentence may carry the product name). Run `pnpm -C packages/client/ui-capability-map run map:build -- --from <file>` for the same effect.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="understand-the-implementation"></a>
+## Understand the implementation
+
+<details>
+<summary>Implementation internals — click to expand</summary>
+
+The rail registers into `shell.rail`, a real grid column the frame declares left of the sidebar, so the rail never draws over the sidebar's pixels. The other left-side seats cannot host it: `sidebar` is a single slot occupied by the navigation column, and `shell.leading` is a single slot occupied by the sidebar's window-chrome controls and mounted only for drawers and collapsed macOS sidebars. The frame's solve collapses an expanded rail to its 48px strip whenever the 320px panel would take the center below its 400px minimum.
+
+The live body subscribes only while the panel is open. It borrows the main-view session's durable event window from the Client Session service and folds four event kinds: `tool/call` starts a step, `tool/result` settles the same call id in place, `turn/end` settles anything still open without clearing the path, and a human `user/message` (`source.kind === 'user'`) starts a new task and clears the path. A session switch or collapsing the rail forgets everything. Steps are keyed by call id, so one invocation is exactly one row even when the start event appears twice.
+
+`daniel_run` (and the argv half of `daniel_write_plan`) resolves its `argv` to a command token: flags are skipped and the first two non-flag tokens are used, so `["workspaces","list"]`, `["account","workspaces","--with-quota"]`, and `["--json","brands","list"]` all resolve. `daniel_batch` resolves its calls; a multi-command batch is one row and only claims a shared module when every call agrees. Dedicated tools resolve through their bridge or their own rule; anything else becomes 其他能力 with business fallback copy, never the model's arguments.
+
+The component holds no view state: `open` is the frame's, and the only controls are the strip and the panel's close button. `Escape` inside the panel calls `onToggle`; focus moves to the close control on open and back to the strip on close. Styles use only `--dsw-*` theme tokens plus the frame's `--dsh-frame-top-clearance`; the running pulse and the task-reset fade are CSS-only and are removed under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
+
+</details>
+
+-----
+
+<a id="further-exploration"></a>
+## Further Exploration
+
+- [Layout slots](../ui-layout/README.md) — the frame's seats, including `shell.rail`.
+- [Slot registry](../ui-slots/README.md) — registration kinds and standard props.
+- [UI primitives](../ui-primitives/README.md) — the icons and shared controls the rail uses.
+- [Sidebar](../ui-sidebar/README.md) — the navigation column the rail deliberately leaves alone.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+None, as the execution rail renders the current task's progress and runs no command, RPC, or model request.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+None; the rail contributes no model input and no content that changes cache layout.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- The rail's column is always present outside drawer mode, so it costs 48px of horizontal space even when unused; on frames too narrow to keep the center's 400px minimum beside the 320px panel, the rail stays a strip and the expand request is deferred to the next wider frame.
+- The rail's top band is not a window drag row: on macOS the traffic lights sit over it and the column starts its content below `--dsh-frame-top-clearance`.
+- Module names and business actions are Chinese business copy from the workflow map; only the rail's chrome is translated.
+- The published table is a build-time snapshot. After the workflow map changes, regenerate it or the rail keeps showing the previous actions.
+- The rail follows the main-view session. Background sessions and subagent activity are not shown.
+- A multi-command `daniel_batch` counts once for its shared module (or for no module when the calls disagree); it does not add one call to every module.
+- View state is intentionally not persisted: the rail always mounts collapsed and forgets its last panel state.
+- Packaging must rebuild Client bundles (`pnpm run build:lib:client`); a Desktop-only build leaves `lib/client.js` absent and the entry cannot load.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Working context for maintainers — click to expand</summary>
+
+The generated module's header records the source digest; compare it with the workflow map before trusting a stale-looking rail. The package ships no host-side behavior.
+
+</details>
