+---
+description: "Model context stating the workspace and brand the browser's top bar has selected, carried by each prompt instead of the message body."
+kind: "package-reference"
+---
+
+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-selection-context
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+## Summary
+
+`dsh-client-selection-context` turns the workspace and brand chosen in the app's top bar into request context. The browser attaches the pair to each prompt as `source.clientSelection` metadata — never as message text — and this plugin states the newest pair as optional runtime context when the request is assembled. A user who only picked the two values and asks which workspace or brand is active is answered from context; switching the selection changes the pair on the next prompt. The row is desktop-only, and a Session whose prompts never carried a pair contributes no context.
+
+## Table of Contents
+
+- [Use this package](#use-this-package)
+- [Understand the implementation](#understand-the-implementation)
+- [Further Exploration](#further-exploration)
+- [Model Experience](#model-experience)
+- [Known Limitations and Deferred Work](#known-limitations-and-deferred-work)
+- [Dev Note](#dev-note)
+
+-----
+
+<a id="use-this-package"></a>
+## Use this package
+
+Mount this plugin when a browser application has an explicit workspace/brand selection and the model should know it without the user repeating it. The browser half is the request-context source registered by the capability map; this package owns the Host half. The pair rides the durable `user/message` source, so a resumed Session replays the same records.
+
+### What the model gets
+
+One runtime-context paragraph names the workspace and the brand with their ids. A Session whose prompts never carried a pair adds nothing.
+
+### Configuration
+
+The minimal mount needs no configuration. The Desktop composition enables the row only for that profile, so other profiles never load it.
+
+## Understand the implementation
+
+<details>
+<summary>Implementation internals — click to expand</summary>
+
+### Design concept
+
+The plugin records the newest pair in an `agent/pre-step` listener, before the step's runtime context is refreshed, and contributes it through `ctx.systemPrompt.context`. The record is a weak per-Session map, so a disposed Session takes its pair with it.
+
+### Source map
+
+| File | Role |
+|---|---|
+| [`src/index.ts`](src/index.ts) | Plugin entry: pre-step recording and the runtime-context provider |
+
+### Main flow
+
+The prompt that carries a pair arrives in the pre-step waterfall. The listener stores it, then the step refreshes registered runtime contexts and renders the paragraph. A changed paragraph becomes one new `runtime-context` snapshot at the history tail; an unchanged paragraph adds no message.
+
+</details>
+
+-----
+
+<a id="further-exploration"></a>
+## Further Exploration
+
+- [Context group map](../README.md) — sibling request-context packages.
+- [Web application bundle](../../bundle/web-app/README.md) — the composition that enables this row for the desktop profile.
+
+-----
+
+<a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Model Experience
+
+### Selected workspace and brand
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+The request carries a four-line paragraph inside the runtime-context snapshot; the user's own message stays verbatim.
+
+##### Selected pair
+
+```markdown
+Current workspace and brand selected in the app's top bar (authoritative for this conversation even though the user's message does not repeat them):
+- Workspace: "jack" (id 90002)
+- Brand: "Halliday" (id 4800023)
+When the user asks which workspace or brand is active, answer with these values. A newer snapshot supersedes these values.
+```
+
+#### Token effect
+
+A fixed paragraph is added only when the pair changes or the Session has no retained snapshot; an unchanged selection adds no request tokens.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Append-only: a new snapshot follows the reusable request prefix, so existing KV Cache entries stay valid.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+<a id="known-limitations-and-deferred-work"></a>
+
+- **Historical snapshots are immutable** — a switched pair appends a new snapshot; the previous one stays in history and is marked superseded rather than rewritten.
+- **Desktop-only row** — the shipped Web composition disables the row, and without the browser selector there is no pair to state.
+- **No inference** — the plugin never guesses a workspace from tool results or directory names; an absent pair stays absent.
+
+<a id="dev-note"></a>
+### Dev Note
+
+<details>
+<summary>Working context for maintainers — click to expand</summary>
+
+None.
+
+</details>
